// Phase 12 Plan 03, Task 3 -- the anti-Pitfall-1 fixture (12-RESEARCH.md's
// Common Pitfalls, Pitfall 1: vacuous exhaustive-dispatch coverage).
//
// Architectural finding, recorded rather than silently worked around
// (D-09-45's stale-reference/finding discipline, applied here to a
// GRAMMAR limit rather than a stale doc): a payload destructure/
// construct pair is ONLY emitted for a BARE-VALUE match arm
// (analyzePayloadArm, D-12-05) -- a bare arm has no braces, so there is
// no linear body inside it in which a `let x = borrow ...` statement
// could ever appear. A BODY arm (`Pattern => { ... }`) CAN contain a
// real borrow sequence (analyzeArmBody, exactly `choose` below), but
// analyzeArmBody does not consult a payload binder at all -- and
// `core.mixed_arm_forms` forbids mixing bare-value and body arms in one
// match regardless. So a payload destructure and an explicit borrow
// statement CANNOT be combined inside the SAME match function this
// phase without extending analyzeArmBody itself (out of this plan's
// declared file scope -- check.go is not in Task 3's file list).
//
// The achievable, still-genuine combination: two functions, ONE program,
// checked and validated together in a single check.Program /
// corevalidate.Validate pass. `choose` is `testdata/phase3/
// branch_one_arm_shared_accept.schway`'s own function, UNCHANGED --  a real
// shared borrow whose last use precedes a sibling arm's plain move,
// driven through checkBranch's loanLivenessFixpoint. `identity` is the
// payload tracer's own function, UNCHANGED -- both new operation kinds,
// driven through the SAME six-site control. Per D-12-32/mixed_body_
// versions, a program may not mix Match-bodied and Linear-bodied
// FUNCTIONS, but both of these are Match-bodied (checkBranch handles
// bare-value and body arms alike), so they coexist in one module without
// tripping that guard -- this is what stops the exhaustive-dispatch
// control from reporting coverage of "payload operations meeting borrow
// machinery" that a construct-then-match-only corpus would not actually
// have earned.

module result.payload_borrow_interaction

export {
  type Switch
  type Fault
  type Outcome
  fn choose
  fn identity
}

data Switch =
  | On
  | Off

data Fault =
  | Broken

data Outcome =
  | Ok(Buffer)
  | Err(Fault)

fn choose(flag: Switch) -> Switch {
  match flag {
    On => {
      let view = borrow flag
      let noted = view
      let moved = take flag
      moved
    }
    Off => {
      let held = take flag
      held
    }
  }
}

fn identity(result: Outcome) -> Outcome {
  match result {
    Ok(v) => Ok(v)
    Err(e) => Err(e)
  }
}
